// Build settings that are not Xcode's to own.
//
// The bundle id and the signing team are NOT here, deliberately. They live as literals in the
// pbxproj because Xcode rewrites them whenever Signing & Capabilities is touched in the UI, so a
// `$(VARIABLE)` in this file is overwritten within one session and the two then disagree silently.
// There is one app, one id and one team, so the shortest honest form wins:
//
//   dev.dubec.monad                  the app, simulator and device alike
//   dev.dubec.monad.CheckInWidget    the Live Activity extension, derived by hand
//   3D6D8LQ6F2                       DEVELOPMENT_TEAM — "Jakub Dubec (Personal Team)"
//
// An extension's id must be its host's plus one dot-separated suffix. Change the app's id and the
// widget's must change with it, or the device build fails to sign while the simulator keeps working.
//
// THE TEAM ID IS NOT THE STRING IN THE CERTIFICATE'S NAME. This repo carried that mistake for
// months, in a comment that told the next reader to copy the wrong value:
//
//   subject= CN=Apple Development: Jakub Dubec (GS862349S6), OU=3D6D8LQ6F2, O=Jakub Dubec
//                                                ^ cert id        ^ TEAM ID
//
// The parenthesised GS862349S6 is the certificate's own identifier. The Team ID is the OU. Read it
// with `security find-certificate -c "Apple Development: Jakub Dubec" -p | openssl x509 -noout
// -subject`, or from Xcode -> Settings -> Accounts beside the "(Personal Team)" row.
//
// `O=Jakub Dubec` also settles a second error this repo repeated: 3D6D8LQ6F2 was described as a
// PAID lab team distinct from a personal one. It is the personal team. There is only one, and
// there never was another.
//
// ENTITLEMENTS, and what changed on 2026-09-18
// --------------------------------------------
// For as long as this build signed with the FREE personal team, the entitlements file was an empty
// dict: an entitlement a team cannot grant is a SIGNING failure rather than a runtime one, so four
// were absent rather than requested. A paid Apple Developer Program membership now exists — App
// Store Connect holds the "Monad Scanner" record — so two of the four are back:
//
//   aps-environment       REQUESTED AGAIN. Push works on iPhone for the first time; the in-app
//                         inbox always did, because it polls GET /api/me/notifications over HTTP.
//                         Needs an APNs .p8 key uploaded to the monad-count Firebase project too.
//   associated-domains    REQUESTED AGAIN, as applinks: + webcredentials: on monad.dubec.dev. The
//                         domain's half is /.well-known/apple-app-site-association and it serves an
//                         EMPTY claim until web.applinks.ios_app_ids is set in monad-knowledge's
//                         config.toml. An empty claim fails silently on the handset.
//   HotspotConfiguration  Still out. Cannot join a Wi-Fi network itself, and there is none to join:
//                         the AX210 fleet cannot be an access point.
//   wifi-info             Still out. Cannot read back the SSID, so a session sidecar records an
//                         empty one. Nothing in the analysis reads that field.
//
// THE TEAM ID BELOW IS NOT YET VERIFIED AGAINST THE PAID MEMBERSHIP. 3D6D8LQ6F2 is the personal
// team's id. An individual enrolment may or may not keep it. Read the live answer from
// Xcode -> Settings -> Accounts, next to the membership row, and if it differs, change it in THREE
// places or the links break silently: DEVELOPMENT_TEAM in the pbxproj, the widget's copy of it, and
// web.applinks.ios_app_ids in monad-knowledge's config.toml (`<TEAMID>.dev.dubec.monad`).
//
// The free team's seven-day provisioning expiry no longer applies. A paid team's development
// profile lasts a year, and a TestFlight build is good for 90 days from upload.
APP_NAME = Monad Scan
OTHER_LDFLAGS = $(inherited) -lsqlite3
ENTITLEMENTS_FILE = iosApp/iosApp.entitlements
